        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8954435c-3794-5614-ab50-148da3cfe94e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giacomo Meyerbeer, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Works: L'esule di Granata\n- Roles: opera composer, composer\n- Topics: nineteenth-century stage composition, Classical era, serious opera\n\nFacts:\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was born on 27 January 1756, was baptised as Johannes Chrysostomus Wolfgangus Theophilus Mozart, and was a prolific and influential composer of the Classical era.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer was born as Jacob Liebmann Beer on 5 September 1791 and was a German opera composer of Jewish birth.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart died on 5 December 1791.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer has been described as perhaps the most successful stage composer of the nineteenth century.\n- L'esule di Granata is a two-act melodramma serio, or serious opera, by Giacomo Meyerbeer.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer died on 2 May 1864.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
